In article <2960EB9F.29108@orion.oac.uci.edu> iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu (Mike Iglesias) writes:

>   In article <1991Dec31.194650.9923@cis.umassd.edu> stoodt@cis.umassd.edu (Michael Stoodt) writes:
>   >On the same subject, I'm wondering how much good it would do to set
>   >the "sticky bit" (chmod 1755, etc.) on the perl executable.  Does
>   >anyone care to comment before I try it?

>   I tried this recently and it didn't seem to make much difference.

I wouldn't expect it to make much difference.  ULTRIX, like the BSD
system it is derived from, keeps program text pages around in memory
until it actually needs to reclaim the memory.  Hence, if you're using
perl a lot, it will probably be in memory.  If it isn't, something
else needed the memory, and the hint of the sticky bit doesn't really
make any difference.

