Hello,
	
	I am having problems initializing an endnode over ddcmp
	attached to our microvax 2.  We wrote our own DDCMP
	device driver.  The DDCMP link seems to initialize fine,
	and then we exchange hello and test messages.

	After the third message, the microvax abruptly goes back
	to DS (data link start) state and drops the connection!

	Here are the clues that we have.  We're stumped.

	1. The vax sent ACKs for each and everyone of our hello
	   messages, no NAKs were sent.  

	2. We sent ACK packets for each of its hello messages

	3. The QSYNC and SELECT flag are both turned on for each
	   of the data messages sent from the vax.  We are running 
	   over an asynchronous line.

	4. After each of the vax's data messages, two 0xf bytes
	   are sent.  This seems to be a "short synchronization".	   

	5. When we use NCP to look at the "characteristics" of the line
	   we are trying to bring up,  the substate is "-synchronizing"
	   throughout the period that we are exchang hello messages.
	   Why is it synchronizing while it is in fact sending hello msgs?
	   After the line goes down, an "initialzation failure" is recorded.
	   Can hello messages be sent durring the intialzation phase of
	   the routing layor?

	6. When the vax brings down the line it first appears to send
	   a "long" synchronization message- that is something like 
	   128 "0xf" bytes.

	Can anyone out there help us diagnose this problem?  Any help,
	hints,  or suggestions,  would be great.  Doccumentation on 
	DDCMP is scarce and we have had to do alot of guesswork.

						Thank you,

