Between local systems I get about 5 megabytes per minute.
No translation is involved in normal usage.  LAT is a remote terminal
protocol, rather nor functional than TELNET and unrelated to FTP.
LAD (LAST) is a remote disk (storage) protocol that is different from
and may be better than NFS or FTP but it not involved unless the files are 
located elewhere on a network connected using it.


